<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Other evaluation protocols</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated the transferability estimation methods based on other rank correlation metrics, including Spearman’s <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> and Kendall’s <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>. As shown in Tab. <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.5 Other evaluation protocols ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices and Supplementary Material ‣ Implicit Modeling for Transferability Estimation of Vision Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, ITM also achieved the best performance on these two metrics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span><span id="A1.T8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison of Spearman’s <math id="A1.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> and Kendall’s <math id="A1.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite> for different methods on various datasets.</span> </figcaption>
<div id="A1.T8.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:122.1pt;vertical-align:-59.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-119.1pt,42.2pt) scale(0.591519077643472,0.591519077643472) ;">
